<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · site</p><h1 class="enc-title">Concepción de la Vega</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1494">1494</a>–<a href="/years/1562">1562</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/15th-century">15th century</a> · Also known as La Vega Vieja</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Concepción de la Vega was a Spanish fortress and town in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vega-real">Vega Real</a> of central <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hispaniola">Hispaniola</a>, founded by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/christopher-columbus">Christopher Columbus</a> in 1494–1495 in the land of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/taino">Taíno</a> chiefdom of Maguá. It grew rich from gold mining and became a bishopric in 1511, but was destroyed by an earthquake in 1562. Its ruins, La Vega Vieja, lie near the modern city of La Vega in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dominican-republic">Dominican Republic</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/concepcion-de-la-vega.jpg" alt="Concepción de la Vega" width="320" height="210" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: CristoRey99 · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:La_Vega_Dominican_Republic_2.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
